            <div xml:id="d192">

                <pb facs="0310" n="192" xml:id="pg192"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.5045/7: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Cafe Haitien</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wood</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cape Haitien</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-05T15:00:00-05:00">December 5, 1929—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Cape Haitien district quiet under martial law. All public demonstrations broken
                    up without casualties.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wood</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
